        // A new state a Move or an erase leaves holding only water (a lake its fill took) is discarded, and the Save then drops every move into it
        // (orphanedQueuedWrites), so the files keep that lake where it was. The page took it out of every state and said "stays where it is, in no
        // state": a lake filled into a new state from state 5 was in no state on the page after the Save and in state 5 on disk, until a reload.
        // Where the Save leaves it: the state its last move that still goes out took it to, or, with none, the one its first move took it from,
        // followed through the merges queued since (a state merged away takes it along); one that came in by a merge goes where that merge was
