  // Classify the rivers.bmp palette into CLEAR paint actions, using the REAL documented HOI4 scheme.
  //
  // ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-09-08 — this comment said "verified on the wiki + the actual MD/vanilla rivers.bmp:
  // land = grey (122,122,122), sea = white" and had it BACKWARDS, which is worse than saying nothing because
  // it claims to have been checked. Measured over vanilla, Millennium Dawn and Old World Blues:
  //
  //   index 254 = rgb(122,122,122)  ~65% of the map, and 99.3% / 99.5% / 99.8% of it lies over SEA provinces
  //   index 255 = rgb(255,255,255)  ~34% of the map — the LAND background, which is where the rivers are
  //                                 (non-background pixels: 450,300 on land against 371 on sea)
  //
  // So grey is the SEA background and white is the LAND background — the opposite way round.
  //
  // ✅ …and it does not matter to the game, which is why nothing ever caught it. The wiki (Map modding,
  // rivers.bmp): "Pixels with any other index within the file do not get read in-game and serve as
  // 'comments', usually used to signify the land province outlines to make it easier to place rivers."
