  // as the grey index because that is what Nova has always written and changing it would alter how existing
  // mods look in an external editor for no in-game gain. Recorded here so the next reader is not misled into
  // "fixing" a bug that is a cosmetic convention.
  //
  // The three river MARKERS are green (0,255,0) = SOURCE/start, red (255,0,0) = flow-IN (a tributary joins another river),
  // yellow (255,252,0) = flow-OUT (a branch); and the river BODY is indices 3–11 (cyan→deep blue), where ≤6 are
  // SMALL rivers (minor crossing penalty) and ≥7 are LARGE / major rivers (the widest = a "giant" river). The
  // old code mislabelled RED as "Source" and never offered the real green source at all. Swatches preview in the
